{
  "_": "MEASURED, not chosen. tools/shadow-audit.js turns one object's castShadow off, renders the LIT frame through the scene's own renderFrame() at a frozen time, and counts the pixels that moved. Every name below moved ZERO. A shadow-casting light draws every caster into its map every frame, so each name here is two draw calls a frame that paint nothing.",
  "_regenerate": "?shadowaudit=1 then window.__shadowAudit.run() at each declared pose, movers hidden AND in frame, union the keepers. Re-run after any re-dress, any sun-angle change, and any new pose. It is an opt-OUT list on purpose: a prop added later casts by default, costing two draws, where an opt-in list would silently lose its shadow.",
  "_controls": "Both controls must pass or the run is refused: changing nothing must move exactly 0 pixels, and killing every shadow must move >= 500. Then the whole drop set is switched off AT ONCE and must still move 0 — a shadow hidden behind another shadow reads zero on its own and only disappears when both go.",
